# Class-groupoid relations from finite data

A `ClassAtlas X` is a finite presentation of an equivalence relation on `X` as the union of the
graphs of finitely many continuous maps defined on closed sets:

`x ~ y ↔ ∃ i (hx : x ∈ dom i), glue i ⟨x, hx⟩ = y`.

This is the shape of the class-groupoid relation `~₁` of the Ratcliffe--Tschantz construction:
the `dom i` are closed faces of the truncated polytope (in the two copies), the `glue i` are the
affine identifications of faces, and the groupoid axioms (cocycle, restriction compatibility to
subfaces, invariance of the pairings) are precisely what makes the displayed relation an
equivalence relation and covers every point.  This file isolates the *topological* consequences of
that data: the graph is closed, hence the quotient is Hausdorff (when `X` is compact Hausdorff),
and openness/closedness in the quotient can be checked on the closed domains.

## How to instantiate it for `~₁`

`X := Q̄₀ ⊔ Q̄₁`; the index type is the set of face classes of the class groupoid (finitely many);
`dom i` is the union of the closed faces in the class; `glue i` is the affine identification of
faces (extended over the union, continuous because the pieces are compact); `rel` is the relation
generated by the identifications.  The two obligations are `rel_iff` (every chain of
identifications collapses to one step — this is where the cocycle and the restriction
compatibility to subfaces are used) and `iseqv`.  The `InvolutionAtlas` presentation below
reduces those two obligations to the finite checks "the pairings are involutions" and "the
composite of two pairings is, on the overlap, again one of them".

Main results:

* `Work.QuotientT2.ClassAtlas.setoid`, `…quotient_mk_eq_iff`, `…class_eq`
* `Work.QuotientT2.ClassAtlas.isClosed_relGraph` (alias `ClassAtlas.isClosed_graph`)
* `Work.QuotientT2.ClassAtlas.t2Space_quotient`, `…compactSpace_quotient`
* `Work.QuotientT2.ClassAtlas.isOpen_quotient_iff`, `…isClosed_quotient_iff`
-/
import Mathlib
import Submission.Work.QuotientT2.Basic
import Submission.Work.QuotientT2.isOpen_iff_forall_isOpen_subtype_of_isClosed_cover
import Submission.Work.QuotientT2.isClosed_iff_forall_isClosed_subtype_of_isClosed_cover

-- Lean v4.35.0-rc3 / Mathlib 5e0c4e5 made `isDefEq` respect transparency when unifying instances; with it,
-- `ZMod.instField` and `ZMod.commRing` (and `Neg (ZMod p)` via `SubtractionMonoid`) no longer unify, which
-- breaks `ring`/`rw`/module-instance search on `ZMod p`. Restore the v4.34 behaviour for this file.
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency false
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.instanceSearchTypes false
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false


open Set Topology Function

namespace Work.QuotientT2

universe u

/-- Finite data presenting an equivalence relation on `X` as a finite union of graphs of
continuous maps on closed sets. -/
structure ClassAtlas (X : Type u) [TopologicalSpace X] where
  /-- Index type of the glue maps. -/
  ι : Type u
  /-- The index type is finite. -/
  [fintype : Fintype ι]
  /-- The closed set on which the `i`-th glue map is defined. -/
  dom : ι → Set X
  /-- The domains are closed. -/
  dom_closed : ∀ i, IsClosed (dom i)
  /-- The glue maps. -/
  glue : (i : ι) → dom i → X
  /-- The glue maps are continuous. -/
  glue_continuous : ∀ i, Continuous (glue i)
  /-- The relation presented by the atlas. -/
  rel : X → X → Prop
  /-- The relation is exactly the union of the graphs of the glue maps. -/
  rel_iff : ∀ x y, rel x y ↔ ∃ i, ∃ hx : x ∈ dom i, (glue i ⟨x, hx⟩ : X) = y
  /-- The relation is an equivalence relation (this is the cocycle/restriction-compatibility
  content of the data). -/
  iseqv : Equivalence rel

attribute [instance] ClassAtlas.fintype

namespace ClassAtlas

variable {X : Type u} [TopologicalSpace X] (A : ClassAtlas X)

/-- The equivalence relation presented by a class atlas. -/
def setoid (A : ClassAtlas X) : Setoid X where
  r := A.rel
  iseqv := A.iseqv

theorem setoid_iff {x y : X} : A.setoid x y ↔ A.rel x y := Iff.rfl

/-- The relation is the union of the graphs of the glue maps. -/
theorem rel_iff' {x y : X} :
    A.rel x y ↔ ∃ i, ∃ hx : x ∈ A.dom i, (A.glue i ⟨x, hx⟩ : X) = y :=
  A.rel_iff x y

/-- Every point lies in some closed domain. -/
theorem exists_dom (x : X) : ∃ i, x ∈ A.dom i := by
  obtain ⟨i, hx, -⟩ := A.rel_iff x x |>.mp (A.iseqv.refl x)
  exact ⟨i, hx⟩

/-- The closed domains cover `X`. -/
theorem iUnion_dom : ⋃ i, A.dom i = Set.univ := by
  ext x
  simp only [mem_iUnion, mem_univ, iff_true]
  exact A.exists_dom x

/-- Two points have the same class iff some glue map sends one to the other. -/
theorem quotient_mk_eq_iff {x y : X} :
    Quotient.mk A.setoid x = Quotient.mk A.setoid y ↔ A.rel x y :=
  Quotient.eq

/-- The class of `x` is the image of `x` under the glue maps whose domain contains `x`. -/
theorem class_eq (x : X) :
    {y | A.setoid x y} = ⋃ i, {y | ∃ hx : x ∈ A.dom i, (A.glue i ⟨x, hx⟩ : X) = y} := by
  ext y
  constructor
  · intro h
    obtain ⟨i, hx, hxy⟩ := A.rel_iff x y |>.mp h
    exact mem_iUnion.mpr ⟨i, hx, hxy⟩
  · intro h
    obtain ⟨i, hx, hxy⟩ := mem_iUnion.mp h
    exact A.rel_iff x y |>.mpr ⟨i, hx, hxy⟩

/-- The graph of the relation of a class atlas, as the union of the graphs of the glue maps. -/
theorem relGraph_setoid :
    relGraph A.setoid =
      ⋃ i, {p : X × X | ∃ hx : p.1 ∈ A.dom i, (A.glue i ⟨p.1, hx⟩ : X) = p.2} := by
  ext p
  obtain ⟨a, b⟩ := p
  simp only [mem_relGraph, Set.mem_ofPred_eq, mem_iUnion]
  exact A.rel_iff a b

/-- **The graph of a class-atlas relation is closed** (for `X` Hausdorff): it is a finite union
of graphs of continuous maps on closed sets. -/
theorem isClosed_relGraph [T2Space X] : IsClosed (relGraph A.setoid) := by
  rw [A.relGraph_setoid]
  exact isClosed_iUnion_of_finite fun i =>
    isClosed_graph_of_continuous (A.dom_closed i) (A.glue i) (A.glue_continuous i)

/-- The name used in the blueprint for `ClassAtlas.isClosed_relGraph`. -/
theorem isClosed_graph [T2Space X] : IsClosed (relGraph A.setoid) := A.isClosed_relGraph

/-- **The quotient presented by a class atlas on a compact Hausdorff space is Hausdorff.** -/
theorem t2Space_quotient [CompactSpace X] [T2Space X] : T2Space (Quotient A.setoid) :=
  t2_quotient_of_closed (r := A.setoid) A.isClosed_relGraph

/-- The quotient presented by a class atlas on a compact space is compact. -/
theorem compactSpace_quotient [CompactSpace X] : CompactSpace (Quotient A.setoid) :=
  Quotient.compactSpace

/-- The quotient presented by a class atlas on a compact Hausdorff space is T₁. -/
theorem t1Space_quotient [CompactSpace X] [T2Space X] : T1Space (Quotient A.setoid) := by
  have := A.t2Space_quotient
  infer_instance

/-- **Openness in the quotient can be checked on the closed domains.** -/
theorem isOpen_quotient_iff {U : Set (Quotient A.setoid)} :
    IsOpen U ↔ ∀ i, IsOpen {x : A.dom i | Quotient.mk A.setoid (x : X) ∈ U} := by
  rw [isOpen_quotient_iff_preimage]
  exact isOpen_iff_forall_isOpen_subtype_of_isClosed_cover A.dom_closed A.iUnion_dom

/-- **Closedness in the quotient can be checked on the closed domains.** -/
theorem isClosed_quotient_iff {U : Set (Quotient A.setoid)} :
    IsClosed U ↔ ∀ i, IsClosed {x : A.dom i | Quotient.mk A.setoid (x : X) ∈ U} := by
  rw [isClosed_quotient_iff_preimage]
  exact isClosed_iff_forall_isClosed_subtype_of_isClosed_cover A.dom_closed A.iUnion_dom

end ClassAtlas

end Work.QuotientT2
